Versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 were published on npm under the MIT License and remain under MIT
for their recipients. This license applies to version 0.2.1 and later.

Without a license key you may install and run the software to scan websites and use the
console gate (console output, exit code, JSON report) in CI, including for commercial and
internal use. Local targets (localhost, loopback) are always free. Local auto-fix (creating
and applying patches in your own working directory, without a commit or pull request) is free
as well.

A valid license from CuonzTech is required for: the PDF report and customer reports (HTML,
Markdown with --client) and auto-fix as a commit or pull request (writing patches into a repository).
The number of domains per plan is based on trust and is not counted by the software.

You may not copy, sell, redistribute or sublicense the software, offer it as your own
product or service, or remove, bypass, disable or forge license checks, license keys or
license notices. Viewing the source code grants no right to modify or redistribute it.

